      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In this study we evaluated quantitatively the contrast enhancement of the myocardium of 27 patients with infarction and ischemia by ultrafast CT (Imatron C-100) with a scan time of 100 msec. We defined three parameters from the CT numbers of the myocardium and the ventricle in both the early and the late phase (about 4 min) after the injection of non-ionic contrast material; the difference of the CT numbers of myocardium between the early and the late phase (delta CT#), and the ratios of the CT numbers of the myocardium and the ventricular lumen (M/L) in both the early phase and the late phase. The delta CT# for myocardial infarction and severe ischemia were -20 +/- 10HU and -8 +/- 10HU, respectively. These values were significantly lower than the mild ischemic myocardium and normal myocardium (p less than 0.001). The average M/L values for myocardial infarction and ischemia in the early phase were 19 +/- 8% and 16 +/- 6%, respectively. These values were significantly lower than those in normal myocardium (p less than 0.001). The average M/L values for infarction and severe ischemia in the late phase were 90 +/- 18% and 63 +/- 20%, respectively. These M/L were significantly dissociated (p less than 0.001). Our results indicate that with contrast UFCT it is feasible to detect quantitatively the myocardial characteristics of ischemia and infarction."},
